{"santizeAnchors implementation is brittle - iterates over anchors and mutates translated value in a way that can misreport or drop anchors if they occur in different order or there are multiple anchors": 0.7020652890205383, "Build-time vs. runtime sanitization enforcement contradiction - finding claims sanitization is only enforced at build time while another finding shows sanitizer is wired into Freemarker rendering at request time, requiring investigation to determine actual enforcement boundary": 0.13387058675289154, "HTML unescaping is applied after sanitization (via StringEscapeUtils.unescapeHtml4 or fixURLs) without re-running the sanitizer, which can reverse the sanitizer's escaping and reintroduce unsafe HTML tags or attributes into the final output": 0.5080340504646301, "Regex in normalizeValue for templateHelp does not account for space before closing angle bracket in CLAIM placeholders (e.g., 'CLAIM.<NAME >'), so placeholders may not be removed, potentially triggering false positives for HTML content in translations": 0.7915456891059875, "HREF_PATTERN regex only matches href attributes with double quotes, ignoring single-quoted href values which may allow some legitimate anchor URLs to bypass the post-sanitization URL unescaping logic (fixURLs)": 0.20700182020664215}